\subsection{The oracle ladder}
Fig.~\ref{fig:ladder} withholds each paper's coarse stage and changes nothing else. The pooled median F1 of \M7 falls from \quadricLzero{} to \quadricLone{}, of \M3 from \lobbLzero{} to \lobbLone{}. Two methods that share nothing but that one input fail by the same factor without it, which makes the honest framing a \emph{ladder every method sits on} rather than a weakness of one. \M4 has one more rung: with the generator's exact normals in place of estimated ones its butt and edge scores rise by about $0.5$, so its mechanism is sound and the normal estimate on a thin coplanar pair is what fails.

